IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part IV, "Regulations": section 108.
-- Written by piece ei3 (Sonnet 5.5). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Unofficial plain-text source; nothing verified
-- against the official text.
--
-- Section 108(1)(a) to (p) is a list of what the Minister may make regulations about, with the approval of the Governor in
-- Council. A regulation-making power is machinery: NOTES.md marks paragraphs (a), (b) and (d) to (p) `inert`, with the reason.
-- Two things in the section are not machinery and are encoded: the figures the Act itself puts on the penalty a regulation may
-- prescribe (paragraph (c)), and the Minister's own powers in subsections (1.1), (2), (3) and (4).
-- The Regulations made under it (the Insurable Earnings and Collection of Premiums Regulations) are not among the inputs.

§ `Section 108(1)(c) - the penalty a regulation may prescribe`

-- "A penalty for non-compliance with regulations made under paragraph (a) or (b) equal to the greater of $100 and the product
-- obtained when $25 is multiplied by the number of days during which the non-compliance occurs, to a maximum of $2,500."
-- src:1761 | (c) prescribing a penalty for non-compliance with regulations made under paragraph (a) or (b) equal to the greater of $100 and the product obtained when $25 is multiplied by the number of days during which the non-compliance occurs, to a maximum of $2,500;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 108(1)(c) (src:1761)
GIVEN `the number of days during which the non-compliance occurs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 108(1)(c) the penalty a regulation may prescribe for non-compliance with regulations made under paragraph (a) or (b)` IS
    IF (25 TIMES `the number of days during which the non-compliance occurs`) GREATER THAN 2_500
    THEN 2_500
    ELSE IF (25 TIMES `the number of days during which the non-compliance occurs`) GREATER THAN 100
         THEN 25 TIMES `the number of days during which the non-compliance occurs`
         ELSE 100

§ `Section 108(1.1) to (4) - the Minister's powers`

-- src:1781 | (1.1) The Minister may authorize an officer or a class of officers to exercise powers or perform duties of the Minister under this Part.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 108(1.1) (src:1781)
GIVEN `the Minister has authorized the officer or a class of officers to which the officer belongs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 108(1.1) the officer may exercise the powers or perform the duties of the Minister under this Part` IF
    `the Minister has authorized the officer or a class of officers to which the officer belongs`

-- Subsection (2): "if the Minister considers that it is not possible to apply any of the regulations, the Minister may, on his or her
-- own initiative or on the request of an employer, approve another method or methods". The Minister's consideration is an input.
-- src:1783 | (2) If the Minister considers that it is not possible to apply any of the regulations, the Minister may, on his or her own initiative or on the request of an employer, approve another method or methods of defining and determining insurable earnings and determining the premiums payable for them.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 108(2) (src:1783)
GIVEN `the Minister considers that it is not possible to apply any of the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 108(2) the Minister may approve another method of defining and determining insurable earnings and determining the premiums payable` IF
    `the Minister considers that it is not possible to apply any of the regulations`

-- src:1785 | (3) The Minister may at any time alter or rescind the approved method, subject to such conditions, if any, as the Minister considers appropriate.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 108(3) (src:1785)
GIVEN `the Minister approved a method under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 108(3) the Minister may at any time alter or rescind the approved method` IF
    `the Minister approved a method under subsection (2)`

-- Subsection (4): regulations under paragraph (1)(p) prescribing or providing for anything mentioned in s 82(1) "take effect on the
-- day they are published in the Canada Gazette or on any later or earlier day specified in the regulations". With no regulation of
-- that kind the subsection says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:1787 | (4) Regulations made under paragraph (1)(p) prescribing or providing for anything mentioned in subsection 82(1) take effect on the day they are published in the Canada Gazette or on any later or earlier day specified in the regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 108(4) (src:1787)
GIVEN `the regulation is made under paragraph (1)(p) prescribing or providing for anything mentioned in subsection 82(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which it is published in the Canada Gazette` IS A DATE
      `a later or earlier day specified in the regulations, if one is` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 108(4) the day on which the regulation takes effect` IS
    IF `the regulation is made under paragraph (1)(p) prescribing or providing for anything mentioned in subsection 82(1)`
    THEN (CONSIDER `a later or earlier day specified in the regulations, if one is`
          WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the day on which it is published in the Canada Gazette`
          WHEN JUST specified THEN JUST specified)
    ELSE NOTHING
